@cindex package-local nicknames
@partofpln

Change the @termrefl{package-local nickname,package-local nicknames}
within @var{package} such that @var{local-nickname} refers to
@var{nicknamed-package} and return the package object designated by
@var{package}.

@var{local-nickname} is a @spectermrefl{string_designator,string
designator} that represents the local nickname to be used to refer to
@var{nicknamed-package}.  @var{nicknamed-package} is a
@spectermrefl{package_designator,designator} for the package object to
be nicknamed.  @var{package} is a
@spectermrefl{package_designator,designator} for a package object to
which the pair of @var{local-nickname} and @var{nicknamed-package} is to
be added.  If @var{package} is not supplied, the current value of
@varref{*package*,@toppackage{}} is used instead.

If the pair of @var{local-nickname} and @var{nicknamed-package} exists in
@var{package} already, then the call to this function has no effect.  If
a pair of @var{local-nickname} and a different nicknamed package exists in
@var{package} already, then an error of type
@classref{nickname-refers-to-different-package-error,@toppackage{}} is
signaled.

